Not really.

Be careful if you say `loading' a font. What you mean is `switching' to a
font. This is a great difference: e.g. the loading-settings in
\DeclareFontShape are executed only _once_ when you really load the font
into TeX's memory. They are not executed afterwards if you switch to this
font again.

Your interface will also fail for nested fonts, as Frank explained to me.

\foo{\bar{...}...}
              ^^^

After leaving the group \selectfont will not be called...

Such a situation cannot happen for my CJK package since I have to select a
new (only in very few cases identical) font for _each_ character.


